## Binding normalization

Use the contact-minimal, then diameter-pair-minimal representative and retain every source point, including contact-isolated points.

The §57 ZR/ZF theorem is only on the nonisolated positive-contact core `V`:

\[
\ker\Omega_V=\operatorname{span}\{\mathbf1,P_x|_V,P_y|_V\},
\qquad
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}[V]=2v-3.
\]

Do not extend this affine-kernel theorem to contact-isolated coordinates. Full-source geometry comes from the separate canonical full-source modules.

## Canonical input to treat as solved

Audit.59 is controlling.

Retain the complete audit.52--58 stack.

Audit.59 adds the adaptive strict-safe saturation theorem.

For any finite deletion set \(R\) and any region
\[
S\subset\operatorname{int}K
\]
with
\[
|y-a|>1
\quad
(y\in S,\ a\in A\setminus R),
\]
one has
\[
\boxed{
E_C(R)=\varnothing
\Longrightarrow
\operatorname{area}S\le a_0|R|,
}
\]
and
\[
\boxed{
E_C(R)\ne\varnothing
\Longrightarrow
\operatorname{area}S\le a_0(|R|-1),
\qquad a_0=\sqrt3/2.
}
\]

For a single contact-active deleted vertex \(v\),
\[
\operatorname{int}K
\subseteq
\bigcup_{a\ne v}\overline B(a,1).
\]

Therefore deleting contact-active guards cannot create net **strict-safe area credit**, even if the deletion set and region are chosen adaptively.

Do not attempt:
\[
\text{delete wall contacts}
+\text{recover collar area}
+\text{average a lattice of spacing }>1
\]
as a closure route. It is canonically blocked.

This does not forbid explicit discrete packets or non-strict packings with exact unit contacts.

## Exact next split

### Full-core branch

Audit.58 reduces suitable finite motions to explicit lower blockers or uncovered anchors. Audit.59 now forces their repair to be genuinely discrete or variational.

Highest-value routes:

1. construct an explicit finite blocker-repair packet with all pairwise/new-old distances checked;
2. exploit exact unit-contact structure rather than strict-safe area to replace deleted wall/anchor points;
3. combine audit.58's distinct blocker matching with audit.53 loaded returns or audit.56 residual-cage coordinates to build a collective non-repacking motion;
4. certify an actual finite packet for audit.54 refill rather than deriving packet count from mean area;
5. prove that failure of every such repair forces an exact unit equilateral triangle.

A result that only increases strict-safe area after deleting contact-active points cannot close the branch.

### Macroscopic inactive-container branch

Same restriction: strict-safe area averaging cannot pay a positive diameter-cover cost after adaptive wall deletion. The remaining capacity must be discrete/exact-contact capacity or come from a different source-level exchange.

